<title>FINLAND: Silja Line Sept passenger volume up 6 pct.</title>
<headline>Silja Line Sept passenger volume up 6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish passenger ferry operator Silja Oy Ab said the number of passengers carried in September by its Baltic Sea operator Silja Line increased six percent year-on-year to 423,300.  </p>
<p>In January-September, Silja Line's passenger volume rose nine percent to 4.6 million people, Silja said in a statement.</p>
<p>It gave the following figures:  Passenger volume (1,000)	   Sept 1996	 change yr/yr</p>
<p> Helsinki-Stockholm		     94,724	    +/-0 pct</p>
<p> Turku-Stockholm			 150,156	     +12 pct</p>
<p> Vaasa traffic			    53,598	     -20 pct</p>
<p> Helsinki-Tallinn			108,320	     +21 pct</p>
<p> Finnjet				    16,538	     +11 pct</p>
<p> TOTAL passengers			423,336		+6 pct</p>
<p> Freight units			    11,341		+5 pct @</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-680 50 245</p>
</text>
